body:
## Game

**Kirby and the Forgotten Land** — title ID `01004D300C5AE000`, built with update **1.1.0 (v65536)** as required by the profile.

## Device and versions

- Device: iPhone (Apple A18 GPU, per log), iOS 26
- NX2Apple v1.3.0, engine pinned `c78d7375`
- Game build: commit `daba995ab521`, shader chain `89f44f9b6bb0`
- IPA built with the Windows builder (shared mode), game data via `romfs.img` in the app group container
- Game language: zh-Hans

## Symptom

The game boots, audio plays, saves mount, and it runs at 60 Hz — but the scene renders **almost entirely black**. Only some effects are visible (e.g. Kirby's inhale effect). The game logic is clearly running underneath (input, audio, FPS counter all fine).

## Log analysis (key excerpts)

All shaders match the shader map (`shader keys not in the shader map (another game version) 0`), so the game/update version is correct. The black screen correlates with many render pipeline creation failures — the fragment shaders write to an integer (`MTLPixelFormatR8Uint`) color attachment, but the inferred outputs are float4, so Metal rejects the pipelines and those draws never render:

```
[dm] [nvn-mtl] [RED] failed to create render pipeline (vertex 5f4b3ec905cfe49e_b fragment f2bad4c3ce41c1e2_b): output of type float4 is not compatible with a MTLPixelFormatR8Uint color attachment.; if its outputs are integers, add to shader_facts_manual.tsv: f2bad4c3ce41c1e2	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
[dm] [nvn-mtl] [RED] failed to create render pipeline (vertex d8d87c2696ad1f9d_b fragment dfcaf654d8910f1c_b): ... dfcaf654d8910f1c	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
[dm] [nvn-mtl] [RED] failed to create render pipeline (vertex d8d87c2696ad1f9d_b fragment 9df52ef750e8bd77_b): ... 9df52ef750e8bd77	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
... (13 distinct fragment shaders in total, all {"fout":{"5":"uint"}})
```

The full list of shader hashes the log asks to add to `shader_facts_manual.tsv`:

```
f2bad4c3ce41c1e2	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
dfcaf654d8910f1c	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
9df52ef750e8bd77	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
77fe5a8328049a01	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
d1ed8276875c09be	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
1071da7f0443ca28	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
a7b3d82d50778443	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
9e45092068edbfb4	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
82564f7aad288df4	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
7248941f5fe8e00e	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
c29bfe207ee10cd8	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
375bb2d591a20ce3	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
2f25facb50821cf5	{"fout":{"5":"uint"}}
```

I tried placing a `shader_facts_manual.tsv` with these lines in `Documents/games/01004D300C5AE000/` on the device, but it did not change the output — it seems the shell does not read it from there. If there is a supported user-override location for `shader_facts_manual.tsv` on iOS, I'd be happy to test it.

Two secondary observations from the same log (may or may not be related):

1. Many repeated `[RED] more than 16 font engines with a small work buffer: this one keeps the game's` lines early in the run — possibly missing in-game text.
2. Several `[RED] texture type mismatch: ... declares slot N as Metal type 2, texture ID ... is type 7 ... bound as is` warnings.

## Full log

Complete `log.txt` from the run: **https://gist.github.com/me2seeks/a2cfd338d98c5ed93e52fde3953e61db**

Happy to test any patch or profile update on this device.

### This is

A problem

### What happens, or what you would like

Rumble never plays on a Switch-mode third-party pad on Mac (GameSir Nova, `057E:2009`, Bluetooth or 2.4 GHz). Core Haptics reports success, but this pad renders only `hapticSharpness = 0`. The host plays 0.5, so games never vibrate. The launcher's Identify plays 0.6, so it is silent too. A genuine Pro Controller rumbles fine through Core Haptics.

A fix that works here: a Pro Controller report route in `dm/host/haptics_apple.m`, next to the DualShock 4 one. It sends HID report `0x10` (HD Rumble) with each motor's own bands, refreshed every 40 ms. `DM_RUMBLE_PRO_REPORT=0` turns it off. The patch is below, with tests.

Launcher: Identify and the rumble test could play sharpness 0 for a Switch Pro Controller.

The route takes every `057E:2009` pad, genuine ones too. It could be limited to pads that fail Core Haptics.

Not checked: a genuine Pro Controller on the report route, two Pro-type pads at once, iOS.

<details><summary>Details</summary>

**Tested on the Nova (Switch mode, macOS 27.2.1):**

| Output | Felt |
|---|---|
| Core Haptics, sharpness 0.5 or 1, any locality, transient taps | no (no error) |
| Core Haptics, sharpness 0 | yes |
| HID report `0x10`, Bluetooth and USB receiver | yes |
| Patched host, Ocarina of Time | yes |

- `dm/host/tests/t_haptics_apple` passes with the new cases: encoding, the route, the refresh, silence, release, the env switch.
- A genuine Pro Controller vibrates normally with the current Core Haptics route.
- The Nova ignores amplitude. Any nonzero step plays at one fixed strength.
- Pairing with two Pro-type pads takes the first free device, as `ds4_take` does.

**Patch** (against engine `c78d7375`, `patch -p1` from the engine root):

```diff
diff --git a/dm/host/haptics_apple.m b/dm/host/haptics_apple.m
index 849af06..564b8fb 100644
--- a/dm/host/haptics_apple.m
+++ b/dm/host/haptics_apple.m
@@ -309,6 +309,117 @@ static BOOL ds4_route(int p, GCController *controller) {
             ds4[p].bluetooth ? "Bluetooth" : "USB", [(__bridge NSNumber *)IOHIDDeviceGetProperty(ds4[p].dev, CFSTR(kIOHIDProductIDKey)) intValue]);
     return YES;
 }
+
+// A Switch Pro Controller, or a controller that presents itself as one (a GameSir Nova in its Switch mode: Nintendo 057E / 2009 over Bluetooth or
+// its 2.4 GHz receiver), is driven through its own rumble report, as SDL's hidapi driver does: 0x10, the packet counter, then four bytes of HD Rumble
+// for the left actuator and four for the right. Core Haptics reaches some of these only at its lowest sharpness: on the Nova (macOS 27.2) every
+// engine and locality started, and only a sharpness of 0 was felt, so a game's rumble (and the Identify of the launcher, at 0.6) never was.
+// The report also plays the game's own bands: its low and high frequencies and amplitudes, per motor, instead of an intensity and a sharpness.
+// DM_RUMBLE_PRO_REPORT=0 keeps such controllers on Core Haptics.
+typedef struct { IOHIDDeviceRef dev; uint64_t id; CFIndex size; uint8_t counter; uint8_t rumble[8], sent[8]; uint64_t generation; } pro_out;   // id: its registry entry
+static pro_out pro[DM_PLAYERS];
+static BOOL pro_report_on = YES;
+static const uint8_t pro_neutral[4] = {0x00, 0x01, 0x40, 0x40};   // 320 Hz / 160 Hz, both silent
+// One actuator's 4 bytes (rumble_data_table.md in dekuNukem's Nintendo_Switch_Reverse_Engineering): frequencies as 32 steps per octave from 10 Hz
+// (high band 0x60-0xDF, from 80 Hz; low band 0x41-0xBF, from 41 Hz), the amplitude as 32 steps per octave too, 0-100, the high band's doubled
+// and the low band's halved over 0x40. A silent actuator gets the neutral bytes, whatever its frequencies
+static void pro_encode(float amp_low, float freq_low, float amp_high, float freq_high, uint8_t out[4]) {
+    float a = fmaxf(amp_low, amp_high);
+    if (!(a > 0)) { memcpy(out, pro_neutral, 4); return; }
+    #define PRO_AMP(x) ((x) <= 0 ? 0 : (x) >= 1 ? 100 : (x) > 0.23f ? (int)lrintf(log2f((x) * 8.7f) * 32) : (x) > 0.12f ? (int)lrintf(log2f((x) * 17) * 16) : (int)lrintf((x) / 0.12f * 16))
+    #define PRO_FREQ(f, lo, hi, dflt) ((int)fminf(hi, fmaxf(lo, lrintf(log2f((isfinite(f) && (f) > 0 ? (f) : (dflt)) / 10) * 32))))
+    int ah = PRO_AMP(isfinite(amp_high) ? amp_high : 0), al = PRO_AMP(isfinite(amp_low) ? amp_low : 0);
+    int hf = (PRO_FREQ(freq_high, 0x60, 0xDF, 320) - 0x60) * 4, lf = PRO_FREQ(freq_low, 0x41, 0xBF, 160) - 0x40;
+    int hf_amp = ah * 2, lf_amp = al / 2 + 0x40 + (al & 1 ? 0x8000 : 0);   // an odd step sets the low band's half step (its byte 2 high bit)
+    #undef PRO_AMP
+    #undef PRO_FREQ
+    out[0] = hf & 0xFF; out[1] = (uint8_t)(hf_amp + (hf >> 8 & 0x01));
+    out[2] = (uint8_t)(lf | (lf_amp >> 8 & 0x80)); out[3] = lf_amp & 0xFF;
+}
+static void pro_send(int p, const uint8_t rumble[8], const uint8_t *sub, size_t sublen) {
+    pro_out *o = &pro[p]; uint8_t r[64] = {0};
+    CFIndex n = MIN(MAX(o->size, (CFIndex)(10 + sublen)), (CFIndex)sizeof r);
+    r[0] = sub ? 0x01 : 0x10; r[1] = o->counter++ & 0x0F; memcpy(r + 2, rumble, 8);
+    if (sub) memcpy(r + 10, sub, sublen);
+    IOReturn e = IOHIDDeviceSetReport(o->dev, kIOHIDReportTypeOutput, r[0], r, n);
+    if (e != kIOReturnSuccess) { if (++errors <= 8 || errors % 64 == 0) fprintf(stderr, "[RED] haptics: Pro Controller rumble report: IOReturn 0x%x\n", e); return; }
+    if (!sub) memcpy(o->sent, rumble, 8);
+}
+// The left actuator plays the game's left motor and the right one its right motor, with the gain and DM_RUMBLE_MIN on each band's amplitude.
+// Resent every 40 ms while it plays: a Pro Controller lets a rumble fade out when no report renews it
+static void pro_apply(dm_haptic_state s) {
+    pro_out *o = &pro[s.player];
+    if (!o->dev) return;
+    for (int m = 0; m < 2; m++) {
+        const dm_vibration *v = &s.motor[m];
+        pro_encode(dm_haptics_apple_controller_intensity(v->amplitude_low * gain), v->frequency_low,
+                   dm_haptics_apple_controller_intensity(v->amplitude_high * gain), v->frequency_high, o->rumble + 4 * m);
+    }
+    uint64_t generation = ++o->generation;
+    BOOL silent = !memcmp(o->rumble, pro_neutral, 4) && !memcmp(o->rumble + 4, pro_neutral, 4);
+    if (silent && !memcmp(o->rumble, o->sent, 8)) return;
+    pro_send(s.player, o->rumble, NULL, 0);
+    if (silent) return;
+    dispatch_after(dispatch_time(DISPATCH_TIME_NOW, 40 * NSEC_PER_MSEC), queue, ^{
+        if (pro[s.player].dev && pro[s.player].generation == generation && s.epoch == dm_haptics_epoch(s.player)) { pro[s.player].generation--; pro_apply(s); }
+    });
+}
+static void pro_silence(int p) {
+    pro_out *o = &pro[p];
+    o->generation++;
+    uint8_t quiet[8]; memcpy(quiet, pro_neutral, 4); memcpy(quiet + 4, pro_neutral, 4);
+    memcpy(o->rumble, quiet, 8);
+    if (o->dev && memcmp(o->sent, quiet, 8)) pro_send(p, quiet, NULL, 0);
+}
+static void pro_release(int p) {
+    pro_out *o = &pro[p];
+    if (o->dev) { pro_silence(p); IOHIDDeviceClose(o->dev, kIOHIDOptionsTypeNone); CFRelease(o->dev); }
+    *o = (pro_out){0};
+}
+@interface DmProChannel : DmRumbleChannel   // one for both actuators; the route takes both motors' values at once (pro_apply)
+@end
+@implementation DmProChannel
+- (void)apply:(dm_haptic_level)level { (void)level; }
+- (void)stop { pro_silence(self.player); }
+@end
+// The first Pro Controller HID device no other player drives, opened for player p, asked of the registry at each connect as ds4_take does.
+// Its rumble is turned on (subcommand 0x48) once it is taken: GameController's own driver leaves it as it found it
+static BOOL pro_take(int p) {
+    CFMutableDictionaryRef match = IOServiceMatching(kIOHIDDeviceKey); io_iterator_t it = 0;
+    if (!match) return NO;
+    CFDictionarySetValue(match, CFSTR(kIOHIDVendorIDKey), (__bridge CFNumberRef)@0x057E);
+    CFDictionarySetValue(match, CFSTR(kIOHIDProductIDKey), (__bridge CFNumberRef)@0x2009);
+    if (IOServiceGetMatchingServices(kIOMainPortDefault, match, &it) != KERN_SUCCESS) return NO;   // takes match
+    BOOL found = NO;
+    for (io_service_t s; !found && (s = IOIteratorNext(it)); IOObjectRelease(s)) {
+        uint64_t id = 0; BOOL taken = NO;
+        if (IORegistryEntryGetRegistryEntryID(s, &id) != KERN_SUCCESS) continue;
+        for (int q = 0; q < DM_PLAYERS; q++) taken |= q != p && pro[q].dev && pro[q].id == id;
+        IOHIDDeviceRef dev = taken ? NULL : IOHIDDeviceCreate(kCFAllocatorDefault, s);
+        if (!dev) continue;
+        if (IOHIDDeviceOpen(dev, kIOHIDOptionsTypeNone) == kIOReturnSuccess) {
+            NSNumber *size = (__bridge NSNumber *)IOHIDDeviceGetProperty(dev, CFSTR(kIOHIDMaxOutputReportSizeKey));
+            pro[p] = (pro_out){.dev = dev, .id = id, .size = size.integerValue > 0 ? size.integerValue : 49};
+            found = YES;
+        } else CFRelease(dev);
+    }
+    IOObjectRelease(it);
+    if (found) {
+        uint8_t quiet[8]; memcpy(quiet, pro_neutral, 4); memcpy(quiet + 4, pro_neutral, 4);
+        static const uint8_t enable[2] = {0x48, 0x01};
+        pro_send(p, quiet, enable, sizeof enable);
+        memcpy(pro[p].sent, quiet, 8); memcpy(pro[p].rumble, quiet, 8);
+    }
+    return found;
+}
+// Only a controller GameController calls a Switch Pro Controller, and only while such a HID device is free
+static BOOL pro_route(int p, GCController *controller) {
+    if (!pro_report_on || ![controller.productCategory isEqualToString:@"Switch Pro Controller"] || !pro_take(p)) return NO;
+    DmProChannel *c = [DmProChannel new]; c.player = p; c.motor = -1; c.target = @"Pro Controller report"; [channels[p] addObject:c];
+    fprintf(stderr, "haptics: player %d controller %s, rumble through the Pro Controller report (%s)\n", p + 1, controller.vendorName.UTF8String ?: "unknown",
+            [(__bridge NSString *)IOHIDDeviceGetProperty(pro[p].dev, CFSTR(kIOHIDTransportKey)) UTF8String] ?: "unknown transport");
+    return YES;
+}
 #endif

 static void native_stop(int p) {
@@ -329,6 +440,7 @@ static void apply(dm_haptic_state s) {
         NSArray<DmRumbleChannel *> *out = channels[s.player];
 #if !TARGET_OS_IPHONE
         if ([out.firstObject isKindOfClass:DmDs4Channel.class]) { ds4_apply(s); return; }
+        if ([out.firstObject isKindOfClass:DmProChannel.class]) { pro_apply(s); return; }
 #endif
         for (NSUInteger i = 0; i < out.count; i++) {
             if (s.epoch != dm_haptics_epoch(s.player)) break;   // a failed channel may replace this route
@@ -351,7 +463,9 @@ static void configure(int p, GCController *controller, GCHapticsLocality localit
     channels[p] = [NSMutableArray new];
 #if !TARGET_OS_IPHONE
     ds4_release(p);
+    pro_release(p);
     if (controller && !locality && ds4_route(p, controller)) { dm_haptics_route(p, 1); return; }   // the report first, as SDL drives it
+    if (controller && !locality && pro_route(p, controller)) { dm_haptics_route(p, 1); return; }
 #endif
     if (controller) {
         GCDeviceHaptics *h = controller.haptics;
@@ -431,6 +545,7 @@ void dm_haptics_apple_output(int p, id owner, dm_haptics_output output) {
             for (DmRumbleChannel *c in channels[p]) [c stop];
 #if !TARGET_OS_IPHONE
             ds4_release(p);
+            pro_release(p);
 #endif
             channels[p]=[NSMutableArray new]; nativeOutputs[p]=[output copy]; dm_haptics_route(p,1);
         });
@@ -462,6 +577,10 @@ void dm_haptics_apple_init(void) {
         if (e) { float v = strtof(e, NULL); if (isfinite(v)) rumble_min = fmaxf(0, fminf(0.9f, v)); }
         e = getenv("DM_RUMBLE");
         dm_haptics_init(apply, !e || atoi(e) != 0);
+#if !TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+        e = getenv("DM_RUMBLE_PRO_REPORT");
+        pro_report_on = !e || atoi(e) != 0;
+#endif
 #if TARGET_OS_IPHONE
         phoneSupported = CHHapticEngine.capabilitiesForHardware.supportsHaptics;
 #endif
diff --git a/dm/host/tests/t_haptics_apple.m b/dm/host/tests/t_haptics_apple.m
index 40fdeb7..3f074eb 100644
--- a/dm/host/tests/t_haptics_apple.m
+++ b/dm/host/tests/t_haptics_apple.m
@@ -166,9 +166,10 @@ static void test_dispatch_after(dispatch_time_t when, dispatch_queue_t target, d
 // A HID device in the fake registry: its entry (one per connection), and the handles made on it
 @interface TestHid : NSObject
 @property io_service_t service;
-@property int product, opens, closes;
+@property int vendor, product, opens, closes;
 @property BOOL bluetooth, failOpen;
 @property NSData *report;
+@property NSMutableArray<NSData *> *reports;   // every report sent to it, oldest first
 @end
 @implementation TestHid
 @end
@@ -184,18 +185,28 @@ static NSUInteger listedNext;
 static int objects;   // iterators and services not released yet
 static TestHid *hid_add(int product) {
     static io_service_t next = 1000;
-    TestHid *h = [TestHid new]; h.service = next++; h.product = product; h.bluetooth = YES;
+    TestHid *h = [TestHid new]; h.service = next++; h.vendor = 0x054C; h.product = product; h.bluetooth = YES; h.reports = [NSMutableArray new];
     [registry addObject:h]; return h;
 }
+static TestHid *pro_hid_add(void) { TestHid *h = hid_add(0x2009); h.vendor = 0x057E; return h; }
+static TestHid *pro_hid_of(int player) {
+    __block IOHIDDeviceRef d; dispatch_sync(queue, ^{ d = pro[player].dev; });
+    return d ? ((__bridge TestHandle *)d).hid : nil;
+}
 static TestHid *hid_of(int player) {
     __block IOHIDDeviceRef d; dispatch_sync(queue, ^{ d = ds4[player].dev; });
     return d ? ((__bridge TestHandle *)d).hid : nil;
 }
 static kern_return_t test_matching_services(mach_port_t port, CFDictionaryRef match, io_iterator_t *it) {
     (void)port;
-    assert(!listed && [(__bridge NSNumber *)CFDictionaryGetValue(match, CFSTR(kIOHIDVendorIDKey)) intValue] == 0x054C);
+    int vendor = [(__bridge NSNumber *)CFDictionaryGetValue(match, CFSTR(kIOHIDVendorIDKey)) intValue];
+    NSNumber *product = (__bridge NSNumber *)CFDictionaryGetValue(match, CFSTR(kIOHIDProductIDKey));
+    assert(!listed && (vendor == 0x054C || vendor == 0x057E));
     CFRelease(match);
-    listed = [registry copy]; listedNext = 0; objects++; *it = SONY_ITERATOR;
+    listed = [registry filteredArrayUsingPredicate:[NSPredicate predicateWithBlock:^BOOL(TestHid *h, NSDictionary *b) {
+        (void)b; return h.vendor == vendor && (!product || h.product == product.intValue);
+    }]];
+    listedNext = 0; objects++; *it = SONY_ITERATOR;
     return KERN_SUCCESS;
 }
 static io_object_t test_iterator_next(io_iterator_t it) {
@@ -220,6 +231,7 @@ static IOHIDDeviceRef test_device_create(CFAllocatorRef a, io_service_t s) {
 static CFTypeRef test_device_property(IOHIDDeviceRef d, CFStringRef key) {
     TestHid *h = ((__bridge TestHandle *)d).hid;
     if (CFEqual(key, CFSTR(kIOHIDProductIDKey))) return (__bridge CFTypeRef)@(h.product);
+    if (CFEqual(key, CFSTR(kIOHIDMaxOutputReportSizeKey))) return (__bridge CFTypeRef)@(h.bluetooth ? 49 : 64);
     assert(CFEqual(key, CFSTR(kIOHIDTransportKey)));
     return (__bridge CFTypeRef)(h.bluetooth ? @"Bluetooth" : @"USB");
 }
@@ -234,6 +246,7 @@ static IOReturn test_device_report(IOHIDDeviceRef d, IOHIDReportType t, CFIndex
     assert(t == kIOHIDReportTypeOutput && id == r[0] && h.opens > h.closes);
     if (![registry containsObject:h]) return kIOReturnNoDevice;
     h.report = [NSData dataWithBytes:r length:n];
+    [h.reports addObject:h.report];
     return kIOReturnSuccess;
 }
 static void drain(void) { dispatch_sync(queue, ^{}); dispatch_sync(queue, ^{}); }
@@ -498,6 +511,66 @@ int main(void) { @autoreleasepool {
     assert(nativeStops && !outputOwners[0] && !nativeOutputs[0] && channels[0].count==1 && [controllerLocalities[0] isEqual:GCHapticsLocalityLeftHandle]);
     dm_haptics_apple_controller(0, nil); dm_haptics_apple_controller(1, nil); drain();
     assert(ds4_crc((const uint8_t *)"123456789", 9) == 0xCBF43926u);   // the report's CRC32 (IEEE, reflected)
+    // HD Rumble bytes (rumble_data_table.md): silence is the neutral 320 Hz / 160 Hz pattern, full is amplitude step 100 on both bands
+    uint8_t e[4];
+    pro_encode(0, 160, 0, 320, e); assert(!memcmp(e, (uint8_t[]){0x00, 0x01, 0x40, 0x40}, 4));
+    pro_encode(0, 41, 0, 1250, e); assert(!memcmp(e, (uint8_t[]){0x00, 0x01, 0x40, 0x40}, 4));   // silent whatever the frequencies
+    pro_encode(1, 160, 1, 320, e); assert(!memcmp(e, (uint8_t[]){0x00, 0xC9, 0x40, 0x72}, 4));
+    pro_encode(1, 160, 0, 320, e); assert(e[1] == 0x01 && e[3] == 0x72);   // the low band alone
+    pro_encode(0, 160, 1, 320, e); assert(e[1] == 0xC9 && e[3] == 0x40);   // the high band alone
+    pro_encode(2, 160, NAN, 320, e); assert(e[1] == 0x01 && e[3] == 0x72);   // clamped, and NaN is silence
+    pro_encode(0.5f, 160, 0.5f, 320, e); assert(e[1] == 0x89 && e[3] == 0x62 && e[2] == 0x40);   // log2(0.5 * 8.7) * 32 = 68 steps: 136 high, 0x40 + 34 low
+    pro_encode(0.305f, 160, 0.305f, 320, e); assert(e[1] == 0x5B && e[3] == 0x56 && e[2] == 0xC0);   // 45 steps: odd, the low band's half step
+    pro_encode(1, 80, 1, 640, e); assert(e[0] == 0x80 && e[1] == 0xC9 && (e[2] & 0x7F) == 0x20);   // an octave up on the high band, one down on the low
+    pro_encode(1, 5, 1, 99999, e); assert(e[0] == 0xFC && (e[1] & 1) == 1 && (e[2] & 0x7F) == 0x01);   // frequencies held to the bands' ranges
+    // A Switch Pro Controller (or a pad presenting itself as one) gets its rumble report while a 057E / 2009 device is free; vibration is turned on once
+    registry = [NSMutableArray new];
+    hid_add(0x05C4);   // a Sony device is not a Pro Controller's
+    TestHid *proBt = pro_hid_add();
+    TestController *sp = [TestController new]; sp.haptics = [TestHaptics new]; sp.productCategory = @"Switch Pro Controller";
+    dm_haptics_apple_controller(0, (id)sp); drain();
+    assert(pro_hid_of(0) == proBt && proBt.opens == 1 && channels[0].count == 1 && [channels[0][0] isKindOfClass:DmProChannel.class]);
+    b = proBt.reports.lastObject.bytes;
+    assert(proBt.reports.count == 1 && proBt.reports[0].length == 49 && b[0] == 0x01 && b[10] == 0x48 && b[11] == 0x01);
+    assert(!memcmp(b + 2, (uint8_t[]){0x00, 0x01, 0x40, 0x40, 0x00, 0x01, 0x40, 0x40}, 8));
+    // Each motor on its own actuator, with the game's frequencies; renewed every 40 ms while it plays, never through Core Haptics
+    dm_vibration_update u2[] = {{0, 0, {1, 160, 0, 320}}, {0, 1, {0, 160, 1, 320}}};
+    dm_haptics_send(u2, 2); drain();
